#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068354 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/id #uuid "369ac89b-e838-5929-ba71-d74b3b06445b" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-10013" :question/problem "Solve the equation $x^2 -10x = -24$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $x^2 -10x +25$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\nx^2 -10x +25 = (x-5)^2\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 10x &= -24 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot x &= -24 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot x + 5^{2} - 5^{2} &= -24 \\\\\n(x - 5)^{2} - 25 &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $25$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 5)^{2} - 25 + 25 &= -24 + 25 \\\\\n(x - 5)^{2} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 5)^{2} &= 1 \\\\\n\\sqrt{(x - 5)^{2}} &= \\sqrt{1} \\\\\n\\mid x - 5 \\mid &= 1 \\\\\nx - 5 &= ± 1 \\\\\nx &= 5 ± 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= 5 - 1 = 4 \\\\\nx_{2} &= 5 + 1 = 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068421 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d78ba1c-5297-5540-afdc-d419d33e0cf7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Rational"}] :question/id #uuid "a0cb3fb6-5ff3-5f4e-9bb9-35c88a22fd34" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-1431" :question/problem "Write the equation $x^2 + 6x +5= 0$ in the form $(x+p)^2=q$, and hence solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + 6x + 5 &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} + 6x &= -5 \\\\\nx^{2} + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot x &= -5 \\\\\nx^{2} + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot x + 3^{2} - 3^{2} &= -5 \\\\\n(x^{2} + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot x + 3^{2}) - 9 &= -5 \\\\\n(x + 3)^{2} - 9 &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 3)^{2} - 9 &= -5 \\\\\n(x + 3)^{2} &= -5 + 9 \\\\\n(x + 3)^{2} &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=3$ and $q=4$. Now, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 3)^{2} &= 4 \\\\\n\\sqrt{(x + 3)^{2}} &= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n\\mid x + 3 \\mid &= 2 \\\\\nx + 3 &= ± 2 \\\\\nx &= -3 ± 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= -3 + 2 =-1 \\\\\nx_{2} &= -3 - 2 =-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Irrational"}] :question/id #uuid "d53f36b5-fc95-55de-b716-789dd327d2f8" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-1432" :question/problem "Solve the equation $x^2-2x-1=0$." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 2x - 1 &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2x &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot x &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} - 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot x + 1^{2} - 1^{2} &= 1 \\\\\n(x^{2} - 2x + 1) - 1 &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} - 1 &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square and solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 1)^{2} - 1 &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} &= 2 \\\\\n\\sqrt{(x - 1)^{2}} &= \\sqrt{2} \\\\\n\\mid x - 1 \\mid &= \\sqrt{2} \\\\\nx - 1 &= ± \\sqrt{2} \\\\\nx &= 1 ± \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our solutions are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= 1 + \\sqrt{2}, \\\\\nx_{2} &= 1 - \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d78ba1c-5297-5540-afdc-d419d33e0cf7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Rational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfa0b688-6fce-58fc-988e-eb15d41877b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=4,\\,x=-4$ and $x=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243037} {:answer/id #uuid "365947dc-402e-5a3f-b3ac-e6696b612205" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=3,\\,x=-6$ and $x=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243038} {:answer/id #uuid "83b19c52-4989-58cf-831b-2b17b33d843d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=3,\\,x=-2$ and $x=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243039} {:answer/id #uuid "56b3793d-ee9e-5827-815a-9edc79cf0013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=6,\\,x=-4$ and $x=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243040} {:answer/id #uuid "9749796f-d628-55cd-b5bb-9017fa3c375c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=4,\\,x=-6$ and $x=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfa0b688-6fce-58fc-988e-eb15d41877b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=4,\\,x=-4$ and $x=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243037} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0b20a5-737e-57da-8567-68d9f0fe9477" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243036}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e4526888-3995-5c7b-92cb-b5eeb975e983" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-112420" :question/problem "The equation ${x}^{2}+6x+8=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $\\,p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+8 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+6x & =-8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3\\cdot x & =-8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3\\cdot x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2} & =-8 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3\\cdot x+{3}^{2})-9 & =-8 \\\\ (x+3{)}^{2}-9 & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square and solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3{)}^{2}-9 & =-8 \\\\ (x+3{)}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=3,q=1,$ and $p+q=4.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3{)}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x+3{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1} \\\\ x+3 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =-3\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3+1=-2 \\\\ x & =-3-1=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-4$ and $x=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d78ba1c-5297-5540-afdc-d419d33e0cf7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Rational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db694b16-0ebe-5b6b-a951-b60a653a5624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$pq=-264\\,$ and $\\,{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=-14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243044} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd923bc-a32e-5d3b-9222-f1df6768ef37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$pq=343\\,$ and $\\,{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=-14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243045} {:answer/id #uuid "a22121fc-7605-5e14-ace2-399261387fff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$pq=-14\\,$ and $\\,{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=49$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243046} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca190bb-5f09-5b2e-bbb6-6947ce63112f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$pq=-343\\,$ and $\\,{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=-14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243047} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ff0da9-065e-5e0d-9c46-1cec8c68dfad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$pq=-343\\,$ and $\\,{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9ff0da9-065e-5e0d-9c46-1cec8c68dfad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$pq=-343\\,$ and $\\,{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243048} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e4805a1-c529-5b08-b948-27428d7a12e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243043}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fac39442-17f5-5ace-9954-931f61698611" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-112457" :question/problem "The equation ${t}^{2}-14t+5=5$ can be written in the form $(t+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $\\,pq\\,,$ and the sum of the roots ${t}_{1}+{t}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-14t+5 & =5 \\\\ {t}^{2}-14t & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-2\\cdot t\\cdot 7+{7}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-7{)}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-7{)}^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=-7$ and $q=49.$ Thus, $pq=-343.$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-7{)}^{2} & =49 \\\\ \\sqrt{(t-7{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ |t-7| & =7 \\\\ t-7 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ t & =7\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} & =7-7=0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =7+7=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum is ${t}_{1}+{t}_{2}=14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Irrational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be4ddca6-67b3-509f-894a-8b3a273075f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243051} {:answer/id #uuid "79c9b9d4-6b32-5de0-8a51-a1c45f39e2f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243052} {:answer/id #uuid "4b46c289-72d7-5e91-8f21-a0e4c11318e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243053} {:answer/id #uuid "d03cd8b4-d9f0-5e20-b907-52f72798a5e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243054} {:answer/id #uuid "5b284b96-2501-5eea-9024-0937edb4bb2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be4ddca6-67b3-509f-894a-8b3a273075f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243051} :answer-field/id #uuid "bba28041-8aba-583a-9230-117d63b45642" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243050}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "208ad88c-bc46-5667-b6d0-efd85dc7c45c" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-112466" :question/problem "The equation ${y}^{2}+4y-9=0$ can be written in the form $(y+p{)}^{2}=q.$   Find $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+4y-9 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}+4y & =9 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot y & =9 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot y+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2} & =9 \\\\ (y+2{)}^{2}-4 & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2{)}^{2}-4 & =9 \\\\ (y+2{)}^{2} & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=2,$ $q=13,$ and $p+q=15.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Irrational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d60c6d70-0501-585c-8560-3ecb2a0fc2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243058} {:answer/id #uuid "0da3aaed-0abe-5b23-a9ad-2e02b94490e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243059} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c759ae-93fa-5283-97a1-385d3836aa69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243060} {:answer/id #uuid "68d9f04e-5ae7-5f9c-8782-1c18150366d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243061} {:answer/id #uuid "c084a2ae-aa99-5873-9885-8ccd52d61d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d60c6d70-0501-585c-8560-3ecb2a0fc2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243058} :answer-field/id #uuid "aef54626-728b-5a7d-8214-c68a30447ad6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243057}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e1edb31-d901-5f73-a61c-d0e033003366" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-112472" :question/problem "The equation ${b}^{2}+14b+14=0$ can be written in the form $(b+p{)}^{2}=q.$   Find $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2}+14b+14 & =0 \\\\ {b}^{2}+14b & =-14 \\\\ {b}^{2}+2\\cdot 7\\cdot b & =-14 \\\\ {b}^{2}+2\\cdot 7\\cdot b+{7}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =-14 \\\\ (b+7{)}^{2}-49 & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b+7{)}^{2}-49 & =-14 \\\\ (b+7{)}^{2} & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=7,$ $q=35$ and $p+q=42.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Irrational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3409b9b3-fc15-515f-828f-a628c5dbcdbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=10,\\,n=-1\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243065} {:answer/id #uuid "7c820b6b-0986-53b4-a63b-dd2658889186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=9,\\,n=-2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243066} {:answer/id #uuid "c25fef68-fbb3-5658-a1bf-bc346ed28955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=11,\\,n=1\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243067} {:answer/id #uuid "7e040d18-b072-5028-92c0-759a0ebf072a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=13,\\,n=3\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243068} {:answer/id #uuid "45e122f6-964e-508f-b1c0-92953e464503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=9,\\,n=1\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25fef68-fbb3-5658-a1bf-bc346ed28955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=11,\\,n=1\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243067} :answer-field/id #uuid "df44da9f-fff4-504a-851d-8a28a7a36640" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243064}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "954a53a0-fe17-5497-8edf-b2cbd6fe7171" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-112488" :question/problem "The equation ${n}^{2}-11=2n$ can be written in the form $(n+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, the $2n$ term to the left-hand side, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-11 & =2n \\\\ {n}^{2}-2n & =11 \\\\ {n}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot n & =11 \\\\ {n}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot n+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2} & =11 \\\\ (n-1{)}^{2}-{1}^{2} & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-1{)}^{2}-{1}^{2} & =11 \\\\ (n-1{)}^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=-1,q=12,$ and $p+q=11.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-1{)}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\sqrt{(n-1{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\ |n-1| & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\ n-1 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ n & =1\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Irrational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3f1d611-aac3-5e70-8fa7-6ce43ecb9137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243072} {:answer/id #uuid "57bca682-aecc-5d9c-bd69-32beda67af72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243073} {:answer/id #uuid "62718a36-e115-5db8-a5a2-ca97b4f0e195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243074} {:answer/id #uuid "25227fd6-030d-5b70-871b-0be18adda881" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243075} {:answer/id #uuid "7808c611-79d3-5d3f-b6d9-fcbbcca2500b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25227fd6-030d-5b70-871b-0be18adda881" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p+q=55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5069923-e6bc-581f-9b55-9d4e811ded5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243071}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46e02905-4bf4-54c0-a32f-d28f800b59c8" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-12995" :question/problem "The equation ${z}^{2}-25=-10z$ can be written in the form $(z+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, the $-10z$ term to the left-hand side, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-25 & =-10z \\\\ {z}^{2}+10z & =25 \\\\ {z}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot z & =25 \\\\ {z}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot z+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (z+5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (z+5{)}^{2} & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=5,q=50,$ and $p+q=55.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d78ba1c-5297-5540-afdc-d419d33e0cf7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Rational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37fa95e0-fa7d-5fec-aa9f-88a4eb40df8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=64,\\,a=-12$ and $a=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243079} {:answer/id #uuid "85ded79c-b9cd-584d-bc84-266e7e52728d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=68,\\,a=12$ and $a=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243080} {:answer/id #uuid "50da7842-a22f-58aa-ab23-0cf66e072979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=60,\\,a=12$ and $a=-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243081} {:answer/id #uuid "6280936c-103a-5995-a127-cb88e7bf1b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=68,\\,a=-12$ and $a=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243082} {:answer/id #uuid "a9137188-8a26-51e8-9692-83ef454a2aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=64,\\,a=-12$ and $a=-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6280936c-103a-5995-a127-cb88e7bf1b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=68,\\,a=-12$ and $a=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243082} :answer-field/id #uuid "50e262aa-c58a-5075-8d70-5f4327bb17f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243078}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4870cb8f-66f0-5759-83b5-334830749092" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-12997" :question/problem "The equation ${a}^{2}+8a=48$ can be written in the form $(a+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+8a & =48 \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot a & =48 \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot a+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =48 \\\\ ({a}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot a+{4}^{2})-16 & =48 \\\\ {(a+4)}^{2}-16 & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+4{)}^{2}-16 & =48 \\\\ (a+4{)}^{2} & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=64,$ and $p+q=68.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+4{)}^{2} & =64 \\\\ \\sqrt{(a+4{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{64} \\\\ a+4 & =\\pm 8 \\\\ a & =-4\\pm 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $a=-12$ and $a=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82128d4e-90ce-54e6-9139-be770a78c0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065693} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c547ca-8084-5908-97de-3f03cc639af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065694} {:answer/id #uuid "e65bf10a-6021-5c9a-b346-04af974d42eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065695} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c4f340-cdf8-5830-8db3-822e954bb964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065696} {:answer/id #uuid "07a9f04a-35e6-50da-82a2-66f5b5f3c581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82128d4e-90ce-54e6-9139-be770a78c0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065693} :answer-field/id #uuid "28535634-27c2-5f2d-8219-b57b1c62ccb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065692}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22f36eaf-d2b6-5e47-8cc3-19f122968355" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-141624" :question/problem "Let $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$ be the solutions of the equation $x^{2} - 2x = 24$. Find the value $x_{1}^{2} + x_{2}^{2}$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $x^{2} - 2x + 1$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x+1=(x-1{)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+{1}^{2}-{1}^{2} & =24 \\\\ (x-1{)}^{2}-1 & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $1$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1{)}^{2}-1+1 & =24+1 \\\\ (x-1{)}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1{)}^{2} & =25 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-1{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\ |x-1| & =5 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =1\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =1-5=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =1+5=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=(-4{)}^{2}+{6}^{2}=52.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d9c6257-ab28-569a-93ed-62492947ecc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243086} {:answer/id #uuid "63aa7789-1eaf-50a9-b251-82e1705cf17a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243087} {:answer/id #uuid "c985eed4-45fd-5335-9a5c-383bfb554305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243088} {:answer/id #uuid "1731cca0-c49f-5e4a-a366-a835aa56ef73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243089} {:answer/id #uuid "b8c8f138-1106-5b1c-8221-4f40ad94794d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63aa7789-1eaf-50a9-b251-82e1705cf17a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243087} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d7b576a-7730-5f9e-a2fe-4a6ba8882703" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243085}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eeb48fe4-90b0-5608-afdb-6e54e437040d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-141804" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ be the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}+4x=12.$ Find the value ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}+4x+4$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+4x+4=(x+2{)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x & =12 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot x & =12 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2} & =12 \\\\ (x+2{)}^{2}-4 & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2{)}^{2}-4+4 & =12+4 \\\\ (x+2{)}^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2{)}^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x+2{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\ |x+2| & =4 \\\\ x+2 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-2\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-2-4=-6 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-2+4=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=(-6{)}^{2}+{2}^{2}=40.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6b9a054-fb5f-580c-9c47-155469005945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243093} {:answer/id #uuid "97a5605b-0ecc-554b-a52a-e3db909c1909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243094} {:answer/id #uuid "a3807fac-4bde-54de-b60a-b3a79189d5a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243095} {:answer/id #uuid "0a96ede7-1e29-5ba5-996f-f6e89f379a38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243096} {:answer/id #uuid "96311a34-81d6-569d-9618-25455f56c8e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6b9a054-fb5f-580c-9c47-155469005945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243093} :answer-field/id #uuid "472e978a-a6d3-5c29-aef2-f78889b6b6ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243092}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a63dfb9f-93e3-51bc-aa25-108f3448b60d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-141812" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ be the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}-8x=20.$ Find the value ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}-8x+16$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-8x+16=(x-4{)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4\\cdot x & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =20 \\\\ (x-4{)}^{2}-16 & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $16$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4{)}^{2}-16+16 & =20+16 \\\\ (x-4{)}^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4{)}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-4{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\ |x-4| & =6 \\\\ x-4 & =\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =4\\pm 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =4-6=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =4+6=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=(-2{)}^{2}+{10}^{2}=104.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e809ade-4805-5a00-9fc5-fca7f7eb86ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243100} {:answer/id #uuid "0e21f58a-d254-5cd3-bd66-e742cf8b1efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243101} {:answer/id #uuid "32046602-5391-5b13-882a-762be049064e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243102} {:answer/id #uuid "a9138edf-cdde-533f-b361-afcdd84e50d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243103} {:answer/id #uuid "d6a46742-4b3d-528e-9d92-9ea072ea5aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32046602-5391-5b13-882a-762be049064e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243102} :answer-field/id #uuid "734e5959-1aa6-5bb3-8c05-d82fcd98b000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243099}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93a225b4-f6a2-5f6f-bfee-a72c21c4b8ec" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-142011" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ be the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}-6x=16.$ Find the value ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}-6x+9$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-6x+9=(x-3{)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\cdot x & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\cdot x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (x-3{)}^{2}-9 & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $9$ to both sides: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3{)}^{2}-9+9 & =16+9 \\\\ (x-3{)}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3{)}^{2} & =25 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-3{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\ |x-3| & =5 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =3\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =3-5=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =3+5=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=(-2{)}^{2}+{8}^{2}=68.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3e24f9c-d383-5b77-a22a-8e142a072f0a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation Given a Corresponding Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92bdf626-02ca-5d11-89da-25cbda1b2c0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243107} {:answer/id #uuid "eef4f0df-56d5-5e6f-be6a-3cb0e359a0b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243108} {:answer/id #uuid "d4236edb-098a-5b3a-bfc8-2b1e51b9428c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243109} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8c0888-2876-5c75-b861-2c0b3e270a66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243110} {:answer/id #uuid "95a07e4a-06e6-5025-83e2-1ae0d8c0c200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95a07e4a-06e6-5025-83e2-1ae0d8c0c200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243111} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ab8cb49-3e23-5850-9310-743eea5320ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243106}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "473e5377-413e-547a-bc5e-d0e683a1b0e3" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-142015" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ be the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}-10x=-21.$ Find the value ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that ${x}^{2}-10x+25$ is a perfect square.*" :question/worked-solution "Using the hint, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-10x+25=(x-5{)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x & =-21 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5\\cdot x & =-21 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5\\cdot x+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =-21 \\\\ (x-5{)}^{2}-25 & =-21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we isolate the perfect square by adding $25$ to both sides: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5{)}^{2}-25+25 & =-21+25 \\\\ (x-5{)}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5{)}^{2} & =4 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-5{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\ |x-5| & =2 \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =5\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-2=3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =5+2=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}={3}^{2}+{7}^{2}=58.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d78ba1c-5297-5540-afdc-d419d33e0cf7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Rational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c682bea-ffc0-513c-a21b-6624e9ee1f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=121,\\,x=-1$ and $x=21$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243114} {:answer/id #uuid "bba6d4c4-1382-535f-90b6-7e37feca6761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=100,\\,x=-11$ and $x=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243115} {:answer/id #uuid "62763fb4-d482-542b-b1c0-6f8a1af4465e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=111,\\,x=-11$ and $x=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243116} {:answer/id #uuid "786349b6-d7e5-5c46-9efa-c46d3fee009e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=101,\\,x=1$ and $x=11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243117} {:answer/id #uuid "f16afde8-4951-5710-bfc0-e153070d1de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=111,\\,x=-1$ and $x=21$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f16afde8-4951-5710-bfc0-e153070d1de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=111,\\,x=-1$ and $x=21$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243118} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3bdb649-16b7-5a07-a1c8-956d3595c6e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243113}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb10d5e7-799c-59f9-9941-681a23b9a8bd" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-30048" :question/problem "The equation ${x}^{2}-20x-21=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $\\,p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-20x-21 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-20x & =21 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 10\\cdot x & =21 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 10\\cdot x+{10}^{2}-{10}^{2} & =21 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 10\\cdot x+{10}^{2})-100 & =21 \\\\ (x-10{)}^{2}-100 & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-10{)}^{2}-100 & =21 \\\\ (x-10{)}^{2} & =121\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=-10,q=121,$ and $p+q=111.$\n\nNow, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-10{)}^{2} & =121 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-10{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{121} \\\\ x-10 & =\\pm 11 \\\\ x & =10\\pm 11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =10+11=21 \\\\ x & =10-11=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-1$ and $x=21.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d78ba1c-5297-5540-afdc-d419d33e0cf7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Rational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86f767c2-4e0b-5c65-bdc0-74f4f9d051e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=29\\,,\\,\\,a=1$ and $a=9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243121} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb7614c-f998-549f-b51e-0f30b1e86f82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=-29\\,,\\,\\,a=1$ and $a=-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243122} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d29bf8-0c33-51eb-9878-198f160be1b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=21\\,,\\,\\,a=1$ and $a=9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243123} {:answer/id #uuid "afc9de7b-9ff3-5070-8862-cbcc7ae0b8c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=29\\,,\\,\\,a=1$ and $a=-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243124} {:answer/id #uuid "42322171-7411-590f-a373-5532e097c98a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=21\\,,\\,\\,a=1$ and $a=-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afc9de7b-9ff3-5070-8862-cbcc7ae0b8c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$p+q=29\\,,\\,\\,a=1$ and $a=-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243124} :answer-field/id #uuid "f144556b-4d18-517f-9a4d-a92e8b834c32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243120}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6941a5b9-c275-5c15-8bac-323a4f9103c3" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-3428" :question/problem "The equation ${a}^{2}+8a=9$ can be written in the form $(a+p{)}^{2}=q.$ Find $\\,p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+8a & =9 \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot a\\cdot 4 & =9 \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot a\\cdot 4+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =9 \\\\ ({a}^{2}+2\\cdot a\\cdot 4+{4}^{2})-{4}^{2} & =9 \\\\ ({a}^{2}+2\\cdot a\\cdot 4+{4}^{2})-16 & =9 \\\\ (a+4{)}^{2}-16 & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+4{)}^{2}-16 & =9 \\\\ (a+4{)}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=25,$ and $p+q=29.$\n\nNow, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+4{)}^{2} & =25 \\\\ \\sqrt{(a+4{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\ a+4 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ a & =-4\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =-4+5=1 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-4-5=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $a=1$ and $a=-9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f04ab7-f6f6-5d01-bfcf-b667e37e4f0b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation When the Solutions Are Irrational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "824db7a0-468b-5b7c-bdd3-7bd19185dd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 80, z =-5 ± 5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066672} {:answer/id #uuid "f44af2a5-1591-5f5e-93ba-40c0ddd584b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 80, z =-8 ± 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066673} {:answer/id #uuid "30dfca08-4199-59da-8d02-2600e0f2122b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 75, z = 5 ± 5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066674} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3b9749-a33c-5c57-89ac-26939f855dba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 80, z = 5 ± 5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066675} {:answer/id #uuid "6d135e5e-ebb4-5c27-84bf-0be68ee6c029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q =-70, z = ± \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "824db7a0-468b-5b7c-bdd3-7bd19185dd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p + q = 80, z =-5 ± 5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066672} :answer-field/id #uuid "988361f0-82f8-5fa0-bce8-8775fead2e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066671}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c0076f5-08a5-5d4c-9789-196650ab8295" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-3435" :question/problem "The equation $z^{2} - 50 =-10z$ can be written in the form $(z + p)^{2} = q$. Find $p + q$, and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, the $-10z$ term to the left-hand side, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-50 & =-10z \\\\ {z}^{2}+10z & =50 \\\\ {z}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot z & =50 \\\\ {z}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot z+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =50 \\\\ (z+5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+5{)}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =50 \\\\ (z+5{)}^{2} & =75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=5,q=75,$ and $p+q=80.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+5{)}^{2} & =75 \\\\ \\sqrt{(z+5{)}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{75} \\\\ |z+5| & =\\sqrt{75} \\\\ z+5 & =\\pm 5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ z & =-5\\pm 5\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
